## English
# CITIZEN DATA PROTECTION & PLATFORM GOVERNANCE LICENSE (CDPGL)
Version 1.0 — 2026

Copyright (c) 2026 Serenity Creativa Labs
All Rights Reserved.

THIS DOCUMENT ESTABLISHES THE LEGAL TERMS AND CONDITIONS GOVERNING SYSTEM DEVELOPMENT, 
SOURCE CODE USAGE, CONTENT, INTEGRITY POLICIES, AND CITIZEN DATA PROTECTION.

================================================================================
SECTION 1: CITIZEN DATA SOVEREIGNTY AND PRIVACY PROTECTION
================================================================================

1. DATA OWNERSHIP:
   All civil identification data, specific personal data, demographic information, 
   and digital activity logs processed, stored, or generated through this system 
   remain the exclusive property of the individual citizens concerned and/or 
   the authorized public governing bodies.

2. PROHIBITION OF EXPLOITATION AND COMMERCIALIZATION:
   Extracting, selling, renting, sharing, or otherwise exploiting citizen data 
   without express legal authorization is strictly prohibited. This includes, 
   without limitation, monetization, unauthorized algorithmic profiling, and 
   third-party advertising integration.

3. SECURITY AND ENCRYPTION STANDARDS:
   Any implementation of the source code contained in this repository must meet 
   the following baseline requirements:
   a. Mandatory encryption of sensitive data in transit and at rest.
   b. Strict prohibition of storing production credentials or live citizen data in 
      public repositories (no hardcoding or plain text storage).
   c. Data Minimization Principle: The system shall only collect and process data 
      strictly necessary for legitimate administrative functions.

================================================================================
SECTION 2: SOURCE CODE LICENSE AND PLATFORM DEVELOPMENT
================================================================================

1. RESTRICTED USAGE LICENSE:
   The source code, system architecture, and development modules in this repository 
   are licensed for review, security auditing, and derived development EXCLUSIVELY for:
   a. The enhancement and delivery of public services.
   b. Responsible academic, technical, and cybersecurity research.
   c. Internal, non-exploitative institutional implementations.

2. ETHICAL USE AND PROHIBITED ACTIVITIES:
   This software SHALL NOT be used, directly or indirectly, to build unlawful mass 
   surveillance systems, discriminatory automated decision-making engines, or any 
   system designed to violate basic human rights and citizen privacy.

================================================================================
SECTION 3: CONTENT, DIGITAL ASSETS, AND INTELLECTUAL PROPERTY
================================================================================

1. CONTENT & MEDIA COPYRIGHT:
   All proprietary content, including technical documentation, workflows, visual 
   assets, iconography, and brand identity elements associated with this platform, 
   are protected under applicable copyright laws. Reproduction, redistribution, or 
   public display without prior written consent from the copyright holder is prohibited.

2. OPEN DATA POLICY (WHERE APPLICABLE):
   Only aggregate public statistics or non-personal metadata explicitly designated 
   as "Open Data" may be made publicly accessible, provided that rigorous, 
   irreversible anonymization techniques are applied to prevent re-identification.

================================================================================
SECTION 4: DISCLAIMER OF LIABILITY
================================================================================

THIS SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED, 
INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A 
PARTICULAR PURPOSE, AND NON-INFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE AUTHORS, DEVELOPERS, 
OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES, DATA BREACHES, OR SYSTEM 
FAILURES RESULTING FROM SERVER MISCONFIGURATIONS, THIRD-PARTY CLOUD INFRASTRUCTURE, 
UNAUTHORIZED CODE MODIFICATIONS, OR OPERATOR NEGLIGENCE OUTSIDE OUR DIRECT CONTROL.

================================================================================
SECTION 5: JURISDICTION AND LEGAL COMPLIANCE
================================================================================

Any breach or violation of these terms shall be subject to civil and criminal liability 
under applicable statutory laws, including but not limited to governing Personal Data 
